  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-13036",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/70eb3f02bc47a4b2b3ea26e20d686e849a36fba58eac4d14da3453d9e3745b45.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\frac{1}{2}$ units **left.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{1}{2}).$",
